# Carom — Audio

This file defines the sounds the game plays, when each one plays, and how muting
behaves. The events themselves are defined by `specs/balls.md` and
`specs/playfield.md`; this file names the sound each one makes.

## Cues

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
A cue is a short sound the game plays by name. The audio layer beneath the game
is yours, so how a cue is synthesized or loaded is your decision; what this file
fixes is the set of cues, their names, and the frame each one plays on.

Play exactly the cues below, under exactly these names:
{{else}}
Audio plays through the runtime's cue bus, which the runtime documents. Define
and play exactly the cues below, under exactly these names, which the seeded
`CUES` constant carries:
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq variant.slug "multi")}}
| Cue | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}Constant | {{/unless}}Played when |
| --- | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}--- | {{/unless}}--- |
| `paddle-hit` | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}`CUES.paddleHit` | {{/unless}}A ball hits a paddle's left or right face. |
| `wall-bounce` | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}`CUES.wallBounce` | {{/unless}}A ball reflects off the top or bottom wall, or off a paddle's end cap. |
| `obstacle-bounce` | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}`CUES.obstacleBounce` | {{/unless}}A ball bounces off an obstacle. |
| `ball-bounce` | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}`CUES.ballBounce` | {{/unless}}Two balls bounce off each other. |
| `score` | {{#unless (eq engine.slug "none")}}`CUES.score` | {{/unless}}A point is scored. |

Each cue is a distinct short blip, so the five events are told apart by ear.

Each plays on the frame its event happens, from the game's update, once on that
frame however many sub-steps or balls raised it. A collision is one event between
two balls, so a frame in which a pair meets plays `ball-bounce` once for the pair.
